<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see sunny, warm weather.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see sunny, warm weather.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Tuesday were forecast to see mainly sunny skies, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see sunny skies with afternoon thundershowers in the south with highs of 27 to 31 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see mainly sunny skies with highs of 25 to 30 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see mainly sunny skies with highs of 25 to 30 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
